One may think that because they are not capable or willing to read what others have written down, there can be no such thing as an accurate representation in which all ideas must fit perfectly together without any hints about how everything will eventually go wrong. However if we consider ourselves more than just humans with limited abilities then perhaps this assumption isn’t completely true afterall;
What does “the world” mean when referring to our existence? Does it refer only toward physical reality where objects exist without meaning but rather something larger encompassing both matter AND spirit within its scope – one which cannot be defined by anything other than itself (e.g., nothing outside).
This leads us back around again: Is there really a way for people who write their thoughts down on paper?
